# Uploads (live content)
uploads/
# backend/uploads is a symlink into /var/lib/quata (runtime data lives
# outside the checkout so a `git clean` cannot delete user files).
# The old !uploads/.gitkeep exception can no longer be satisfied.
backend/uploads

# pnpm lockfile.
#
# Ignored deliberately, not by oversight — but read this before relying on it.
# A committed lockfile is what makes an install reproducible: without one,
# every deploy re-resolves the dependency tree and can pick up a different
# patch release than the build that was tested. That is a real risk, and the
# usual advice is to commit it.
#
# It is ignored here because this repo has never tracked one, deploys already
# install fresh, and adopting a lockfile generated on a developer machine
# would change what actually installs on a live product. Committing it is the
# better end state — it just needs to be a deliberate change, verified on one
# product at a time, rather than a side effect of tidying `git status`.
pnpm-lock.yaml
